</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned.
However, we still want to generate "Out" to provide animation!
===================================================
CONVERT LINTs TO DINTs
===================================================
These COPies and BTDs take the input LINTs and break them into a
pair of DINTs each, then take the low-order signed DINT and breaks it
further into two 16-bit values so we can do unsigned compares on them.

Logix V17 has a LINT data type, but math instructions
(and AOI Input and Output Parameters) don't support LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_Inp_A[2],2)COP(Inp_A,Wrk_Inp_A[0],2)BTD(Wrk_Inp_A[0],16,Wrk_Inp_A[3],0,16)BTD(Wrk_Inp_A[0],0,Wrk_Inp_A[2],0,16);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_Inp_B[2],2)COP(Inp_B,Wrk_Inp_B[0],2)BTD(Wrk_Inp_B[0],16,Wrk_Inp_B[3],0,16)BTD(Wrk_Inp_B[0],0,Wrk_Inp_B[2],0,16);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines the overall LINT "LES" result.
If the Inp_A 32-bit (signed) upper longword is less than that
for Inp_B, then A is less.
If the two signed 32-bit upper longwords are equal,
compare the next 16-bit (unsigned) values.  If A is less,
then LINT A is less.  If these values are equal,
then compare the lowest-order 16-bit (unsigned) values.
If A is less, then LINT A is less.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_Inp_A[1],Wrk_Inp_B[1]) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp_A[1],Wrk_Inp_B[1]) [LES(Wrk_Inp_A[3],Wrk_Inp_B[3]) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp_A[3],Wrk_Inp_B[3]) LES(Wrk_Inp_A[2],Wrk_Inp_B[2]) ] ]OTE(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare inputs and output TRUE if Inp_A < Inp_B]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_LES : 64-bit Less Than
============================================================
Revision 1.0-01 Release:  2010-01-26
Deleted unused Local Tag
============================================================
Compares two LINT (signed 64-bit) inputs (Inp_A and Inp_B) and returns
TRUE if Inp_A is less than or equal to Inp_B, FALSE otherwise.

This instruction breaks the LINT inputs into three DINTs
(32 bit signed, 16 bit unsigned and 16 bit unsigned) to do the comparison.
===================================================
CONVERT LINTs TO DINTs
===================================================
These COPies and BTDs take the input LINTs and break them into a
pair of DINTs each, then take the low-order signed DINT and breaks it
further into two 16-bit values so we can do unsigned compares on them.

Logix V17 has a LINT data type, but math instructions
(and AOI Input and Output Parameters) don't support LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_Inp_A[2],2)COP(Inp_A,Wrk_Inp_A[0],2)BTD(Wrk_Inp_A[0],16,Wrk_Inp_A[3],0,16)BTD(Wrk_Inp_A[0],0,Wrk_Inp_A[2],0,16);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_Inp_B[2],2)COP(Inp_B,Wrk_Inp_B[0],2)BTD(Wrk_Inp_B[0],16,Wrk_Inp_B[3],0,16)BTD(Wrk_Inp_B[0],0,Wrk_Inp_B[2],0,16);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines the overall LINT "LES" result.
If the Inp_A 32-bit (signed) upper longword is less than that
for Inp_B, then A is less.
If the two signed 32-bit upper longwords are equal,
compare the next 16-bit (unsigned) values.  If A is less,
then LINT A is less.  If these values are equal,
then compare the lowest-order 16-bit (unsigned) values.
If A is less, then LINT A is less.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_Inp_A[1],Wrk_Inp_B[1]) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp_A[1],Wrk_Inp_B[1]) [LES(Wrk_Inp_A[3],Wrk_Inp_B[3]) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp_A[3],Wrk_Inp_B[3]) LES(Wrk_Inp_A[2],Wrk_Inp_B[2]) ] ]OTE(Out)OTE(EnableOut);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_LIM" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2008-04-15T14:24:48.205Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2010-01-26T17:36:37.092Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Limit Test (Circular) (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Deleted unused Local Tag]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction compares a 64-bit Input with a 64-bit High Limit and a 64-bit Low Limit.

There are two cases: a "normal case" (Low Limt <= High Limt) and a "circular case" (Low Limit > High Limit)
In the normal case, EnableOut and Out are set if:
    Low Limit  <= Input <= High Limit
In the circular case, EnableOut and Out are set if:
    Input >= Low Limit   OR  Input <= HighLimit  (remember, High Limit < Low Limit !)

This instruction may be used in Ladder Diagram, Structured Text
or Function Block Routines just like the LIM instruction
is used for 32-bit integers and floating point numbers.  However,
because it has InOut Parameters (references to Tags of LINT type),
it is NOT left-justified on ladder rungs!

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="LoLim" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer Low Limit Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer input for compare]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="HiLim" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer  High Limit Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result 1 if Inp is within limits (circular)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LINT_LEQ" DataType="L_LEQ">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for L_LINT_LEQ instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LINT_LES" DataType="L_LES">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for L_LINT_LES instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LINT_GEQ" DataType="L_GEQ">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for L_LINT_GEQ instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that the High Limit is less than the Low Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that Inp is less than or equal to the High Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that Inp is greater than or equal to the Low Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned.
However, we still want to generate "Out" to provide animation!
============================================================
DO THE 64-BIT COMPARES AND RECORD RESULTS
============================================================
This rung performs all the 64-bit integer (LINT) comparisons needed and
records the results for use in the next rung.  Needed results are:

1.  Is HiLim less than LoLim?
2.  Is the Input less than or equal to HiLim?
3.  Is the Input greater than or equal to LoLim?]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[L_LES(Wrk_LINT_LES,HiLim,LoLim) OTE(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) ,L_LEQ(Wrk_LINT_LEQ,Inp,HiLim) OTE(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) ,L_GEQ(Wrk_LINT_GEQ,Inp,LoLim) OTE(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
BASED ON RESULTS, DETERMINE OUTPUT
============================================================
The upper input branch is the normal comparison case, where LoLim  <= HiLim:
True if    ( LoLim  <=  Inp )  AND  ( Inp  <=  HiLim )

The lower input branch is the "circular" (reversed limits) case, where LoLim > HiLim:
True if    ( LoLim  <=  Inp )   OR   (Inp  <=  HiLim )]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) XIC(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) XIC(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) [XIC(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) ,XIC(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ] ]OTE(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare inputs and output TRUE if Input is within Limits (circular)]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_LIM:  64-bit Limit Check (Circular)
============================================================
Revision 1.0-01 Release:  2010-01-26
Deleted unused Local Tag
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if:

when HiLim >= LoLim:      LoLim <= Inp <= HiLim
when HiLim < LoLim:      Inp >= LoLim   OR   Inp <= HiLim
(circular comparison -- see LIM instruction documentation for details!!!)
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
DO THE 64-BIT COMPARES AND RECORD RESULTS
============================================================
This rung performs all the 64-bit integer (LINT) comparisons needed and
records the results for use in the next rung.  Needed results are:

1.  Is HiLim less than LoLim?
2.  Is the Input less than or equal to HiLim?
3.  Is the Input greater than or equal to LoLim?]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[L_LES(Wrk_LINT_LES,HiLim,LoLim) OTE(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) ,L_LEQ(Wrk_LINT_LEQ,Inp,HiLim) OTE(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) ,L_GEQ(Wrk_LINT_GEQ,Inp,LoLim) OTE(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
BASED ON RESULTS, DETERMINE OUTPUT
============================================================
The upper input branch is the normal comparison case, where LoLim  <= HiLim:
True if    ( LoLim  <=  Inp )  AND  ( Inp  <=  HiLim )

The lower input branch is the "circular" (reversed limits) case, where LoLim > HiLim:
True if    ( LoLim  <=  Inp )   OR   (Inp  <=  HiLim )]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) XIC(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) XIC(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) [XIC(Wrk_Inp_LE_HiLim) ,XIC(Wrk_Inp_GE_LoLim) ] ]OTE(Out)OTE(EnableOut);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="L_GEQ"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="L_LEQ"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="L_LES"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
